Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 15:29:56 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(quest): Phase 3.2 (path filter + schema-gap criteria)

Four pieces in one batch:

1. URL-hash path filter (spec section 9.2 wired). New hook
   client/src/hooks/useActivePathHash.ts syncs filter state to
   #path=investor and exposes pathToElement() mapping. The portals
   in PathProgressionSection now persist their selection across
   reloads via the hash. EpicQuestSection subscribes and filters
   sortedQuests by element when a path is active (player=fire,
   investor=water, land_project=earth, ally=air).

2. Land Project Steward criterion (spec section 3.3). Migration
   drizzle/0135_path_steward_criteria.sql adds two columns to
   applications: seasonsCompleted INT DEFAULT 0 and gameLaunchedAt
   TIMESTAMP NULL. tierDetector.checkLandProjectSteward returns met
   when at least one of the user's applications has seasonsCompleted
   >= 1 AND gameLaunchedAt IS NOT NULL. Forward-only: existing rows
   default to 0 / NULL so no retroactive grants.

3. Alliance Partner Co-Creator criterion (spec section 3.2). Reads
   regenTools where submittedBy = userId AND status = 'approved',
   then groups regenToolClicks by toolId counting DISTINCT userId.
   Fires met when any approved tool has 11 or more distinct users.
   Single grouped query rather than N+1.

4. Hypha bonus-claim cascade (spec section 5) was already wired in
   webhook-receiver.ts cascadeClaimPassed (commit d0d2e5b on main).
   Verified end-to-end; no additional code needed in this batch.

No behaviour change for Sage criterion or Alliance Partner Steward
criterion; both still need their own schema work and stay stubbed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
